{start_of_verse: Verse}
Well, [F]good morning, Holy [F/C]Spirit.
Lord, I [F]thank You for another day. [C7]
Won’t You [F]guide me and keep my paths straight?
I need You, Lord, to esta[Bb]blish [F]me and [Bb]give [C]me [F]strength!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[C]All throughout the [C/E]day I want my [Bb]mind to [F]stay on [Csus]You. [C]
[C]Let Your Spirit [C/E]lead me and I’ll [Bb]fol[F]low.
[Em]Oh [Am]Lord, I only want to be [Em]walking in Your [F]will,
So [Dm]I will remember these [Csus]words: [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I’m going to [F]pray [C]without [F]ceasing;
I will [Bb]rejoice for[F]ever[C]more.
I’ll in [C]ev’rything give [C/E]thanks, for this [Bb]is the [F]will [C]of [F]God.
No, I [F]won’t quench the Spirit; I won’t de[Bb]spise prophe[C]cy.
I’m gonna [Csus7]test all things, hold fast to what is good;
I will ab[Bb]stain [F]from [Bb]ev’[F]ry [Csus]e[C]vil.
So that the [Bb]God of peace [C]Him[F]self
Will sancti[Bb]fy me com[C]pletely.
So my [Bb]spirit, soul, and body [F]be saved [C]blameless
To the [C7]coming of our [F]Lord!
To the [C7]coming of our [F]Lord!
To the [C7]coming of our [F]Lord! [Csus7] [C]
{end_of_chorus}
